From f60a669173cc5c897ef80eb449e961f821666e4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:10:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Now playing: a key and a panel for the media player

Command = "NowPlaying" is a key that shows only while the helper reports
a media player with a track (/run/tiny-dfr/bridge/nowplaying, "key value"
lines: status, title, artist, length, position and when it was read, rate,
whether it can seek); hidden it takes no room. A tap opens a panel right
of Esc, as on macOS: a round close button, previous / play-pause / next
(drawn, the middle one follows the status) and a capsule with title,
artist, elapsed / total time and a scrubber. The time runs on from the
last report while playing, redrawn once a second (only the capsule).
Dragging the scrubber shows the new time and seeks on release ("seek
<0..1>"); the keys send "media previous|playpause|next", or media keys
without the helper. Only Esc stays usable under the panel; it closes with
its button, when the player goes, or when the row changes.

The PNG preview shows the key and the panel with a made-up track, and a
key slider opening to the right of its key.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
